speechtext:
1.	For a copy of the address to His Majesty the King, which was adopted by this house, in or about the month of May, 1919, dealing with the conferring of titles of honour or titular distinctions, decorations or orders, upon His Majesty's subjects domiciled or ordinarily resident in Canada, in the form in which said address was transmitted to His Majesty;
2.	For copies of all correspondence between the government of Canada and His Majesty's government at Westminster, or any member thereof, relating to the said address;
3.	For a copy of the King's regulations prescribed by or in the name of His Majesty, dealing with or referring to the acceptance by His Majesty's subjects of titles of honour, titular distinctions, decorations or orders, which may be conferred or proposed to be conferred by any foreign government, governmental authority, state, power or potentate;
4.	For a list of persons domiciled or ordinarily resident in Canada, who, since May 1, 1919, have been the recipients of any foreign title, titular distinction, decoration or order from any foreign government, govermental authority, state, power or potentate; stating the nature of the title, distinction, decoration, or order so conferred in each case; also stating whether approval of the acceptance of such title, distinction, decoration or order by such recipient was signified by or in the name of His Majesty; and also stating whether and in what cases such approval as aforesaid was refused by or in the name of His Majesty to any such recipient; and also stating specifically the names of those domiciled or ordinarily resident in Canada who, since May, 1919, have accepted any such foreign title, distinction, decoration or order, without approval thereof signified by or in the name of His Majesty.
